<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Ala ibn Mughith</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 763</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Ala ibn Mughith was an Arab leader in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> who in 763 raised the black banner of the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Mansur against the Umayyad emir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-i">Abd al-Rahman I</a>, gathering support in the south-west of the peninsula. Abd al-Rahman besieged and defeated him near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carmona">Carmona</a> and killed him, and according to the chroniclers sent his preserved head eastwards as a warning to the caliph.</p></div>
